  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 110 PM CDT Mon Jul 6 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will result in mainly hot and dry conditions \nthrough most of the work week. Highs through much of the work week \nwill be in the mid 90s to near 104, with overnight lows in the 70s. \nDry conditions will also continue Wednesday through Friday. \n\nAs we head into the weekend an upper level ridge will strengthen \nacross the Gulf, with another upper level ridge across the Southwest \nUnited States. This will place Texas in a shear zone between the two \nridges. In addition, the ECMWF is showing an inverted trough \ntracking northwest across South Texas this weekend. These factors \nwill result in slightly less hot temperatures along with a return of \nrain chances. Expect mainly diurnally driven showers and \nthunderstorms, with low to medium (20-40%) rain chances.",
